Wrong (B): This describes Recovery Time Objective (RTO), which measures how quickly a system must be restored to full operation after a failure, not the acceptable data loss window.
Wrong (C): This describes Mean Time Between Failures (MTBF), a reliability metric measuring the average interval between system failures, not data loss tolerance.
