  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under COBIT 2019 DSS01 (Managed Operations), system availability is calculated as MTBF / (MTBF + MTTR), representing the proportion of total time the system is operational. This formula correctly produces the availability percentage needed for SLA reporting.
Wrong (A): MTTR / MTBF calculates an incorrect ratio that does not represent availability. This formula lacks the proper denominator representing total time.
Wrong (B): MTBF minus MTTR produces a time duration in hours, not a percentage ratio. Availability must be expressed as a proportion of total operational time.
Wrong (C): MTTR / (MTBF + MTTR) calculates the unavailability ratio, which is the proportion of downtime rather than the availability metric required.$EXPL$
